# Rule 02. No raw HTML tags outside the kit

Language-agnostic. Zones, `{kit}` and the terms in this rule are defined in rule 00.
The syntax of each term per stack is in the runtime appendix.

## Goal

Atoms emit tags. Screens compose atoms. Only the kit knows which host tag is
used for which role.

## Zones

| Zone | Raw HTML |
| --- | --- |
| Kit: `{kit}` (`packages/<rt>/ui/src/primitives`, `src/utils`) | Allowed. Host markup lives here and only here. |
| Document frame (the single entry HTML file of an app) | Allowed, document skeleton only. |
| Composition (blocks, composite components, screens, templates) | Forbidden. Only components imported from the kit or other composites, plus the structural constructs of the runtime. |

## Rules

1. Composition files contain zero raw native tags for layout, typography,
   lists, forms or controls.
2. Only the runtime's own structural constructs are allowed besides components:
   fragments, slots, conditionals and loops of the current stack.
3. No raw HTML injection and no dynamic tag in composition. Both choose host
   markup, which is the kit's job.
4. Every needed tag is searched in this order:
   1. the primitives of `{kit}`;
   2. the tag groups in the utils of `{kit}`;
   3. if still missing, add and export a new primitive (its spec, for a
      generated kit), then use it. Never fall back to a raw tag in a screen.
5. Do not fake one primitive with a chain of utility classes on another.
6. Do not hand-edit generated files. Change the spec, the authoring builder or
   the emitter instead.

## Substitutions

| Instead of raw | Use |
| --- | --- |
| `div` | `Box`, `Stack`, `Group` or `Grid` |
| `p`, `span`, `h1` to `h6` | `Text`, `Inline`, `Title` |
| landmarks | `Block` with a required `tag` |
| `ul`, `ol`, `li` | `List`, `ListItem` |
| `form`, `label`, `input` | `Form`, `FormItem`, `Label` and the kit input primitives |
| `button`, `a` styled as a button | `Button` with `variant` and `size` |
| card surface | `Card` |

These names are the reference set. Always confirm the real list in `{kit}`.

## Validation

`bun run check`, group `rules`, scans every composition file (never the kit) and fails on a new:

- `raw-native-tag`: an element whose tag is a lowercase HTML or SVG element name;
- `raw-html`: raw HTML injection;
- `dynamic-tag`: a host tag chosen from a value.

The report has file, line and the offending tag. Existing violations are in
`rules/baselines/<package>.json`; the count may only go down.
